<title>BELGIUM: EU declines specific comment on German gold plans.</title>
<headline>EU declines specific comment on German gold plans.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission on Friday said it was awaiting further details on Germany's plan to revalue gold reserves in order to fulfil the Maastricht Treaty's deficit and debt criteria.</p>
<p>&quot;We are waiting to see what the details are,&quot; a Commission spokesman said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said  the EU executive was pleased to see German Finance Minister Theo Waigel was doing all he could to qualify for the single currency, but said EU accounting rules would be &quot;applied strictly&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be no fudging of the figures,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>It was unclear whether a ruling by EUROSTAT, the EU's statistical watchdog, would be needed on the proposed plan, he added.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
